    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling matchups, headlined by **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.97) and **Seiya Suzuki** (65.29), our strongest starts of the day. **Soderstrom** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Rea, while **Suzuki** exploits a positive platoon split against Springs. **Austin Riley** also warrants attention; despite facing a 4.40 xERA arm, his elite BvP history (+8% boost) and situational stability push his score to 63.69. Notably, we are keeping **Corbin Carroll** (61.03) in the lineup despite a daunting matchup against Ohtani; his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon, and the projected order advantage helps mitigate the risk of the ace starter.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros** (50.27), who fell just shy of displacing our lower-scoring assets. While **Karros** profiles as a strong option against the vulnerable Ure\u00f1a, the uncertainty surrounding his lineup spot\u2014officially pending at the time of calculation\u2014forced our hand to favor the confirmed spots of **Alex Freeland** and **Jose Caballero**. We must maintain caution with **Gabriel Moreno**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino**, all of whom face significant SP skill penalties due to the high-caliber arms of Ohtani and Burns. While **James Wood** brings immense value with a 0.407 xwOBA and a prime lead-off spot against Meyer, our focus remains on protecting the categorical floor provided by **Brice Turang** and **Travis Bazzana** as we navigate the scarcity of SB opportunities. With **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Mickey Moniak** remaining sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin, placing a premium on the performance of our daily starters.",
